{% macro pool_classification(examples, legends, marker, legacy_aliases=false) -%}
{% if legacy_aliases %}
{{ anchor("pool-based-al-strategies") }}

.. _pool-based-active-learning-classification:

{% endif %}
{{ heading("Single-output Classification", marker) }}

One annotator gives one class label per selected sample, and each cycle
acquires one sample. The upper plot shows the utilities, the classifier's
decision boundary, and the selected sample. The lower plot shows the test
accuracy of this run. Runs with other data or seeds can give noticeably
different curves.

{{ legend(legends["pool-classification"]) }}

{{ gallery(examples["pool-classification"]) }}

{{ heading("Single-output Classification with Batch Queries", marker) }}

Each cycle acquires four samples. Panel *i* shows the utilities for the
*i*-th selection in the batch. All panels use the same classifier and labels.

{{ legend(legends["pool-classification-batch"]) }}

{{ gallery(examples["pool-classification-batch"]) }}

{{ heading("Multi-label Classification", marker) }}

One annotator gives a complete vector of binary labels for each selected
sample. These examples acquire one vector per cycle. The three panels share
the utilities and show a separate decision boundary for each label. In each
panel, class 0 means that the label is absent and class 1 means that it is
present. Gray markers identify samples whose label vectors have been
acquired.

{{ legend(legends["pool-multilabel"]) }}

{{ gallery(examples["pool-multilabel"]) }}

{{ multiple_annotators(examples, legends, marker, legacy_aliases) }}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro pool_regression(examples, legends) -%}
One annotator gives a continuous label for each selected sample. Two plots
show the fitted regression curve and the utilities. Examples acquire one
sample per cycle unless their caption names a batch.

{{ legend(legends["pool-regression"]) }}

{{ gallery(examples["pool-regression"]) }}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro stream_classification(examples, legends) -%}
One annotator gives one class label per queried sample. Samples arrive in
sequence, and the strategy decides within its budget whether to request each
sample's label. The animation shows arriving samples and the evolving
decision boundary.

{{ legend(legends["stream-classification"]) }}

{{ gallery(examples["stream-classification"]) }}
{%- endmacro %}
